# Normalize every text file to LF, both in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for
# Windows default) re-expands every text file to CRLF on disk. That is
# invisible for source files, but this repo has several tests that compare a
# freshly-generated string against a committed fixture byte-for-byte —
# `test/tool/scoring_fixtures_test.dart` against
# `functions/test/fixtures/scoring_parity.json` chief among them (P14's
# cross-language parity fixture). The generator always writes LF; a CRLF
# working copy then fails that comparison on Windows alone, even though the
# committed blob (and every other platform's checkout of it) is unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf
